{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Only be strong, not to eat the blood.</b> From the fact that it says חֲזַק, you learn that they were steeped in blood to eat it; therefore it was necessary to say חֲזַק — the words of Rabbi Yehudah. Rabbi Shimon ben Azai says: the verse comes only to warn you and teach you how much you need to strengthen yourself in the commandments. If blood, which is easy to guard against, for a person does not crave it — nevertheless it was necessary to strengthen you with its warning, how much more so for the rest of the commandments (see Sifrei)." "<b>And you shall not eat the soul with the flesh.</b> A warning against a limb from a living animal (Ḥullin 102)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:50.081356628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}